{:tier :glm-5.2, :verse 7, :comments [{:quotes [{:he "משם נסעו הגדגדה", :translit "misham nas'u hagudgudah", :gloss "from there they journeyed to Gudgodah"} {:he "הפסוק מתחיל במ' ומסיים במ'", :translit "ha-pasuk matchil be-mem u-mesayem be-mem", :gloss "the verse begins with mem and ends with mem"}], :mechanisms [{:kind :other, :note "Letter-geographic frame: the verse opens and closes with the letter mem (מ), taken as an allusion to מ' (40) years."}], :frame {:text "The Well that accompanied Israel in the desert is identified as the rock from which water flowed; it traveled with Israel throughout the forty years of wandering (Numbers 21:16–18). The Targum (Targum Onkelos, Numbers 21:16–18) identifies the 'Well' as the rock-miracle. The Talmud (Ta'anit 9a; also Shabbat 35b) states the Well was given through the merit of Miriam and accompanied Israel for all forty years in the wilderness.", :sources ["Numbers 21:16–18" "Targum Onkelos Numbers 21:16–18" "Ta'anit 9a" "Shabbat 35b"]}}], :arithmetic [{:kind :other, :note "Letter-geographic frame: the verse opens and closes with the letter mem (מ), taken as an allusion to מ' (40) years.", :by :selah, :ran? false}], :book :deuteronomy, :voice :baal-haturim, :lang :en, :chapter 10, :discipline "bht-chalkboard-v1", :timestamp "2026-07-12T23:35:34.395474380Z", :model "glm-5.2"}